title: International Relations
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: international_relations_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; international_relations_timer += 12;
card-image: img/international.jpg
max-visits: 4

Through the Party of European Socialists and the Progressive Alliance, we work with our sister parties across Europe and the world.

- @fr_uk: Work with the French Socialists and British Labour.
- @scandi: Learn from the Danish and Spanish social democrats, who are still winning elections.
- @comintern: Build bridges with the European left beyond social democracy.
- @america: Build ties with the Democrats in the United States.
- @return: We do not need international contacts at the moment.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@fr_uk
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; west_relation += 1; reformist_strength += 5; moderate_plan_support += 1

With a Labour government in London and the Socialists strong in Paris, our sister parties can help us move Europe on investment and defence.

@scandi
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: reformist_strength += 4; labor_strength += 4; investment_support += 1; resources -= 1; moderate_plan_support += 1

The Danish social democrats won back workers with a hard line on migration, while the Spanish socialists won with rising wages and strong public investment. Our factions draw very different lessons from them.

@comintern
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; linke_relation += 5*(1-dissent); linke_coalition += 1 if comintern_seen == 0; comintern_seen += 1; reformist_dissent += 3

Through European left networks, we build contacts with the Linke's sister parties and with the Linke itself. The Seeheimer are not pleased, but the old suspicions begin to fade.

@america
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; us_relation += 1

The Democrats are in opposition and divided, but they are useful contacts in Congress and in the states.
